ent evictions. Alternatively, we can parse the capacity from the command line or default it to 2 to match the GUI\'s default.\n\n### Suggestion on Revision\n\nModify the CLI execution block to use a default capacity of 2 (matching the GUI default) so that evictions actually occur and can be verified, or allow the capacity to be optionally specified. Since the prompt specifies sys.argv[1] contains the semicolon-separated commands, we should default the capacity to 2.\n\nHere is the corrected __main__ block:\n\npython\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    # If command line arguments are provided, run in CLI mode\n    if len(sys.argv) &gt; 1:\n        commands_input = sys.argv[1]\n        # Use a default capacity of 2 (matching the GUI default) to allow eviction testing\n        capacity = 2\n        output = run_commands(commands_input, capacity=capacity)\n        print(output)\n    else:\n        # Otherwise, launch the GUI\n        root = tk.Tk()\n        app = LRUCacheGUI(root)\n        root.mainloop()\n'} |
